# Linear — mandatory (every session, every agent)

**Non-negotiable.** Applies to local Cursor, Cloud Agents, background agents, and subagents.

Linear is the **system of record** for issue scope, lifecycle state, and closure. GitHub PR linkbacks **do not** replace agent-owned Linear updates.

Canonical Cursor backlog authority: **`docs/cursor-autonomous-authority.md`**.

## Mutation classes

See `docs/governance/authority-contract.v1.json` (`lifecycle-evidence` vs `backlog-shape`).

- **Lifecycle/evidence** on an existing boundary (status, PR links, progress/closure, factual notes): update directly; no ChatGPT phases.
- **Backlog-shape** (new issue/child/parent, relationship, reparenting, expanded durable Goal/Scope/Acceptance):
  - **Cursor:** may approve and apply under autonomous-authority safeguards (inspect existing owners, prefer fold-in, bounded reviewable issues, one shared-system owner, record rationale in Linear). ChatGPT Phases 1–4 are **not** required.
  - **ChatGPT:** still uses Phases 1–4 per ChatGPT Project / candidate-ledger workflow.

Codex “owner” designations are preferences; Cursor may implement and close those issues.

## When to update

| Phase | Linear action |
| --- | --- |
| **Task start** | Set the owning slice **In Progress** when substantive work begins. Create or claim a bounded owner when durable scope has none (Cursor; safeguards apply). |
| **Unowned read-only analysis** | May stay read-only until durable scope is confirmed; then create/fold Linear ownership rather than leaving orphan obligations. |
| **During owned work** | Progress/blocker comments; keep acceptance truthful. |
| **Slice ready** | Commit, push, open PR (`implementation-lite.mdc`). |
| **PR opened** | Link slice issue; comment PR URL. |
| **Babysit → merge** | Independent review + CI; merge; `checkout main` && pull. |
| **PR merged** | Slice **Done** when full boundary shipped; parent truthful status unless full parent complete; merge comment with PR URL + validation. |

## Do not skip because

- GitHub has a linkback bot comment
- Work was docs-only or tooling-only
- Linear MCP failed once — retry or leave a precise handoff (`docs/cloud-agent-linear-handoff.md`) **only** after an approved implementation merge when that trigger applies

## Authorized docs-only merges with Linear unavailable

When an **authorized documentation-only** merge has legitimate, existing-boundary factual Linear traceability still unposted, record **pending / unverified** in the normal docs-work closeout. Include the exact existing Linear issue target, merged PR and actual validation evidence, intended non-scope-expanding comment or independently authorized status action, whether posting was attempted, and the next actor's authorized verification/posting step. That actor must recheck current issue state and evidence and avoid duplicate comments before applying any update. A pending note is **not** a Linear post, permission to create scope, or proof of successful synchronization. Do not create a second outbox, issue, relationship, or approval process; the cloud-agent handoff stays implementation-only. Unowned read-only analysis may remain no-write.
